WEBVTT

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:15.640
Reset it once.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.250
Shall I convert this to numeric values?

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.320
It looks like that won't be necessary.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.390
It's plain as day.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.660
Yes...

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.330
Though they're brother and sister, they're different.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.710
Just as I thought, Tatsuya.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.410
You have amazing power locked inside you.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.190
It's nothing to fear, just because you're different from other people.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.450
This is a special power.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.460
Special power?

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.790
Yes, special.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.760
Kiyoko...

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:48.140
All finished?

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.370
Yeah...

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.290
<i>Look!</i>

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.530
<i>No fair!</i>

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.890
<i>Over here!</i>

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:11.650
<i>Hurry up and take it!</i>

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.430
<i>Whoa... wait!</i>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.700
<i>Here it is, Toru.</i>

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.070
<i>Give it to me, hurry!</i>

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.670
<i>Hurry!</i>

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.290
Isamu!

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.560
Thank you!

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.450
What's wrong?

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.780
It's nothing. I guess it was just my imagination.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.190
Toru!

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.010
The ball...

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.550
Thank you.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.400
What was that, just now?

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.140
I just put Dynamis into him.

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:58.430
Dynamis?

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.970
If you do this, power passes to the other person.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.780
Will you try doing it for me?

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:18.620
Well?

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.120
Nothing...

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:25.550
You don't seem to have a fever.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.130
That's why I told you, that kind of stuff is a trick.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:32.760
Yeah...

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:52.820
Hey, it's a new piano!

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.920
You had one of those, the same as that.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.060
A tuning fork?

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.230
What does that sound mean?

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:10.740
You use that as a standard for tuning.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:15.510
It's an "A" tuning fork, so you match the "la" sound to it, and then...

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:22.680
That's it, you check the tones one by one as you make chords, like that.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.550
Huh...

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:28.390
Hey, when the piano's done, teach me to play, okay?

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:30.600
You said you'll teach me, right?

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.960
Oh, but...

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:36.400
You're worried about what happened last time?

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.870
There's no reason to worry about each little thing SHE says.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:46.210
Toru?

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:49.340
The kid's been wound tight nonstop recently.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:54.380
I never told him to keep himself hyper-aware around the clock.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:59.590
But Toru knows you're hoping for that from him,

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.720
...because he's that kind of kid, more than you know.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:08.860
Certainly, to say I don't expect a lot from Toru's sensing abilities would be a lie.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:14.270
I gave him power to replace what was depleted, but that's about all I can do.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:19.140
If he keeps it up, he'll go completely to pieces before Gilgamesh comes.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.700
What a fine big brother!

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.320
Will you show me the data on that wing?

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:40.420
All of it, even what we looked over before.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.260
As you wish, my lady.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.260
Music, my lady?

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.940
Only during the night will be fine.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:53.610
Just for while the children are sleeping,

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:56.910
...I want you to create a sound field to surround the hotel.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:00.520
Also, arrange for measuring devices that search for changes in frequency.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:04.610
As many as possible, ones that can gauge minutely.

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:08.290
If their physical structure is this different,

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:12.590
...their absorption and dispersion of various frequencies will naturally differ too.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:16.560
By those changes we'll detect intrusions?

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.530
My lady, what music shall we play?

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:26.370
I leave that to you. Work it out with the hotel's people.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.170
Just don't play that piece.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:33.880
My lady?

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.390
That concerto from before.

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:49.360
You don't have to press that hard, more gently.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.970
This is hard. Oh, whatever.

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:06.220
Don't do that!

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:07.480
Good, huh?

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:45.760
This was originally a hymn. It's a song that sings of the joy...

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:48.920
...of being reunited with loved ones near a beautiful river in Heaven.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.560
It is?

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:43.340
This should make things a bit easier for you.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:48.110
You can sleep with me tonight.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:50.680
Okay!

00:11:56.490 --> 00:11:57.690
Studying?

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:07.100
Yeah, I wanted to know what Dynamis is.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:10.700
There's nothing written in books about us.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:24.620
In Greek it's "Dynamis." In English it's "power."

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:28.730
Power... Why is that kind of power...

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:29.850
Who knows?

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:35.200
It seems certain that there's a causal relationship with Twin X.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.790
You don't wonder about it?

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:42.410
We were born this way. There's nothing we can do about it.

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:45.780
The Countess was saying that fighting with Gilgamesh is your appointed task.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:49.870
She said if you died doing that, it would fulfill your greatest wish.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:52.510
I wish she wouldn't take it upon herself to kill us off like that.

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:55.210
It's not my greatest wish.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.890
Then why?

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.150
Maybe it's because I have nothing better to do.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:08.430
Compared with us, aren't you the one for whom it's inevitable?

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:10.990
Inevitable?

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:16.070
You have a reason to take them on. Them, and the one who's behind them.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:29.750
Welcome back. Where were you?

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:31.190
Oh, you know...

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.490
What are you thinking about?

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:36.790
Huh?

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:40.160
Nothing.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.000
Shall we see if I can guess?

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.100
You were thinking about Dad!

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:18.970
You could tell?

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:21.340
I understand everything about you, Tatsuya,

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:24.780
...even without using that kind of power or anything.

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:28.950
Kiyoko, you were saying you remember a little about Dad.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:29.970
What kinds of things?

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:34.480
Playing piano together, and...

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:50.830
Let's stop with this Dad stuff.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.570
You have your sister. You're not lonely, right?

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:00.670
No...

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:53.860
I'm sorry, somehow I relaxed too much.

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.870
It's all right. Get dressed.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:13.980
An intrusion?

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:18.620
I don't know. There's no sign anywhere. Just an error?

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:23.080
It could be. I'll look into whether we can specify a location.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.460
You take a look around in the meantime.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:30.720
You two, go back to your room immediately.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:45.920
Tatsuya, get the lights!

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:47.140
Okay...

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:01.760
Isn't this...

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:09.200
Kiyoko!

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:14.500
Hey...

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:20.010
Here...

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:31.550
Really? Glad I made extra.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.100
Won't you sit?

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:53.010
How about it? Are you comfortable at the Hotel Providence?

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:58.310
Caring service, pleasant spaces, and the finest dinners.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:00.550
We're not lacking anything.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:06.250
If it's true, that's good. But you look lonely somehow.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:10.480
You didn't have that kind of cloud over you last time.

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:12.860
Stop giving us that bull!

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:16.130
I think you yourselves realize it the most.

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:26.430
There's not a single thing you need here, only meaningless junk.

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:30.010
You're aware of that, right?

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.890
Let's go, to our place.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.650
No.

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:46.290
Anyway...

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.120
Anyway?

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:50.400
I'm...

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:56.140
...not lonely or anything.

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:03.380
I'm not lonely.

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:05.120
Kiyoko!

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.550
You too.

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.780
You're coming with us, right?

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:13.950
Let's go, then.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:36.010
Kiyoko!

00:20:44.690 --> 00:20:46.120
Don't go!

00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:59.130
What is this?

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:09.240
Kiyoko...

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.880
Kiyoko! Kiyoko!

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:20.290
Kiyoko!

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:27.990
I didn't think Dad would stoop so low,

00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:29.690
...since he's made an enemy of the entire world anyway.

00:23:29.690 --> 00:23:31.320
Is there anything as cruel as this?

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.460
Always, everywhere, that mirror is looking down on us.

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:35.990
Let's stop running. It's all the same.

00:23:35.990 --> 00:23:38.300
It's not like we can escape from this sky anyway.

00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:40.930
To restore the universe's peace and order?

00:23:40.930 --> 00:23:42.230
Well, that's splendid self-promotion, anyway!

00:23:42.230 --> 00:23:43.870
What's that about, after all this time?

00:23:43.870 --> 00:23:48.370
Conquer the world, destroy the Earth, Dad can do just as he pleases.

00:23:48.370 --> 00:23:50.110
What do you know?!

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:53.270
It's somehow as if we're in a bad dream that goes on and on.
